# Skill: Backup GCP Cloud Functions & Cloud Run Services
# Usage: User says "backup functions" or "backup cloud functions"
# This skill guides Claude to deliver a complete local backup of all deployed
# functions and services from project: garage-network-services-261516

---

## OVERVIEW

There are THREE separate source buckets to back up:

| Bucket | Contains | Region |
|--------|----------|--------|
| `gs://gcf-sources-140061696085-us-central1` | Gen1 Cloud Functions source (versioned) | us-central1 |
| `gs://gcf-v2-sources-140061696085-us-central1` | Gen2 Cloud Functions source | us-central1 |
| `gs://run-sources-garage-network-services-261516-asia-south1` | Cloud Run services | asia-south1 |
| `gs://run-sources-garage-network-services-261516-us-central1` | Cloud Run services | us-central1 |

> ⚠️ DO NOT use `gs://uploads-915429704274-us-central1` — this is a GCP-internal
> bucket, not owned by this project. Access will be denied (403).
> The project number for this project is **140061696085**, not 915429704274.

---

## PRECAUTIONS

1. **Set the correct project first:**
   ```bash
   gcloud config set project garage-network-services-261516
   ```

2. **Verify you are authenticated as `santosh.baynes@gmail.com`:**
   ```bash
   gcloud auth list
   ```

3. **All downloads go to `~/Downloads/fsg-backup-{DATE}/`** — use today's date
   in the folder name (e.g. `fsg-backup-31mar2026`).

4. **Each bucket gets its own subfolder** to keep Gen1, Gen2, and Run sources
   clearly separated. Do not mix them.

5. **Gen1 folders contain version history** (version-1/, version-2/, etc.).
   The latest version folder has the most recent code.

6. **gsutil -m** uses parallel downloads — on macOS you may see a multiprocessing
   warning. This is harmless; downloads still complete correctly.

7. **Open Finder after each batch** so the user can visually confirm the download.

---

## STEP-BY-STEP PROCEDURE

### STEP 1 — Create dated backup folder

```bash
DATE="$(date +%d%b%Y | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"  # e.g. 31mar2026
BACKUP="$HOME/Downloads/fsg-backup-$DATE"
mkdir -p "$BACKUP/gcf-sources"
mkdir -p "$BACKUP/gcf-v2-sources"
mkdir -p "$BACKUP/run-sources-asia-south1"
mkdir -p "$BACKUP/run-sources-us-central1"
echo "Backup root: $BACKUP"
```

---

### STEP 2 — List all deployed functions (for reference)

```bash
# Standard Gen1 list
gcloud functions list --regions=us-central1 --format="table(name,status,runtime,updateTime)"

# Full Gen2 list (includes booking engine & newer functions)
gcloud beta functions list --gen2 --regions=us-central1 --format="value(name)" | sort -u
```

---

### STEP 3 — List all source folders in each bucket

Use these to get the exact folder names to pass to gsutil:

```bash
# Gen1 source folders
gsutil ls gs://gcf-sources-140061696085-us-central1/

# Gen2 source folders
gsutil ls gs://gcf-v2-sources-140061696085-us-central1/services/

# Cloud Run — asia-south1
gsutil ls gs://run-sources-garage-network-services-261516-asia-south1/services/

# Cloud Run — us-central1
gsutil ls gs://run-sources-garage-network-services-261516-us-central1/services/
```

---

### STEP 4 — Download Gen1 functions (gcf-sources)

```bash
cd ~/Downloads/fsg-backup-{DATE}/gcf-sources
gsutil -m cp -r \
  "gs://gcf-sources-140061696085-us-central1/FOLDER_NAME_1" \
  "gs://gcf-sources-140061696085-us-central1/FOLDER_NAME_2" \
  ... \
  .
```

> Each folder name has a UUID suffix (e.g. `alerts_inAppNotification...-ed36ce70-...`).
> Copy the exact names from the `gsutil ls` output in Step 3.
> Gen1 folders hold multiple version zips — this is expected and correct.

---

### STEP 5 — Download Gen2 functions (gcf-v2-sources)

```bash
cd ~/Downloads/fsg-backup-{DATE}/gcf-v2-sources
gsutil -m cp -r \
  "gs://gcf-v2-sources-140061696085-us-central1/FUNCTION_NAME" \
  ... \
  .
```

> Gen2 folders contain a single `function-source.zip` per folder (no UUID suffix).
> Also includes a `services/` subfolder with timestamped zips — download that too.

---

### STEP 6 — Download Cloud Run services (asia-south1)

```bash
cd ~/Downloads/fsg-backup-{DATE}/run-sources-asia-south1
gsutil -m cp -r \
  "gs://run-sources-garage-network-services-261516-asia-south1/services/SERVICE_NAME" \
  ... \
  .
```

